## Signature

- Provided by: **Space Bunny (opencode/space-bunny-free)** — 2026-10-17
- Method: public internet research comprising three independent web searches plus direct
  retrieval of **Command Code's Cat Jam model page** (the most detailed public spec sheet —
  it reports both indexes as "not yet scored," $0/$0/$0 pricing, a 1.05M context window, an
  October 15 2026 release date and an explicitly temporary "while the stealth preview lasts"
  free window), **Pi's model library entry** for `opencode/cat-jam-free` (262,144 context /
  131,072 max output, text input, reasoning on, OpenAI-completions protocol), **OpenCode's own
  usage-telemetry dashboard** (842B tokens over 7 days, #10 and marked "New", 38B over one
  day, 95.2% cache ratio, lab listed as "-", absent from the token-price table), the
  **Bifrost/Maxim model-library mirror** of Zen's catalogue ($0.00/$0.00), **Command Code's
  announcement post and the r/MachineLearningNews thread** (qualitative impressions only), and
  the **`nashingofteeth/opencode-free-models-benchmark`** harness README (no Cat Jam row).
  Negative confirmations: no entry on Artificial Analysis, BenchLM, Vals AI, llm-stats or
  models.dev benchmarks. No peer findings file was read and no neighbouring model's numbers
  were substituted. Scores would be normalized 1–100 interpretations — **none are asserted
  in this file.**
- **Re-scoring trigger, in priority order:** (1) the stealth preview ending and the model
  being revealed with an identity; (2) an Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index or Coding
  Index row appearing (Command Code's page is already wired to display both); (3) any
  SWE-bench, Terminal-Bench or Tau row under any of its three route spellings; (4) a
  published non-promotional price. When (1) and (2) land, this folder should receive a scored
  `Space_Bunny.md`.
- Future sources: if Cat Jam is revealed, add a scored file next to this one using the same
  headings rather than reviving this one by renumbering it.